    "seed_text": "Chengdu University of Technology (CDUT, 成都理工大学) — official international admissions excerpts.\n\nUndergraduate (Chinese-taught, 4 years):\n- Non-Chinese citizens, age 18-26, high school graduate, HSK Level 4 or above.\n- CSCA (China Scholastic Competency Assessment) required; score report deadline 30 May 2026.\n- Online application: https://cdut.at0086.cn/student\n- Tuition: Liberal Arts RMB 4,500/year; Science and Engineering RMB 5,000/year.\n- Accommodation: RMB 1,500/person/year (4-6 students/room).\n- Insurance: RMB 800/year. Registration fee: RMB 600.\n- Scholarships: Sichuan Provincial Government Scholarship; Chengdu Municipal Government Scholarship; CDUT living allowance RMB 800/month for 10 months/year.\n- Contact: College of International Education, oshc@cdut.edu.cn, (028) 84073357.\n\nPostgraduate (Chinese and English taught; master 3 years, PhD 4 years):\n- Master tuition: Liberal Arts RMB 18,000; Science & Engineering RMB 19,800 per year.\n- Doctoral tuition: Liberal Arts RMB 22,000; Science & Engineering RMB 24,000 per year.\n- Accommodation RMB 1,500/year; insurance RMB 800/year.\n- CSC High-level Postgraduate Program Type B, university code 10616. Coverage: tuition, stipend, insurance, on-campus housing.\n- English-taught: IELTS 6.0 or TOEFL 80 (non-native). Chinese-taught: HSK 4+.\n- CSC application typically until 1 March 2026."
